REM dhancha — instantiate a new FAKIR domain on the spine
REM targets PANINI spec as published at zistgah/panini; check with ops/pni_check.sh
CYCLER "dhancha"
TITLE "Instantiate a domain"
OUTPUT KIND SPINE
RESOLUTION EASY

STAGE CONCEPT
  VERB CREATE
  SHAPE TEXT
  ASK <<
    Name the domain and the one capability it abstracts.
    Not the field it belongs to — the capability. "Communication engineering" is a
    field; "acquire, transform and deliver a signal across a link whose geometry is
    changing" is a capability.
    Then name the FAKIR lattice point: ISIC section, ISCO major group, ISCED field,
    and which AGI layers L0-L9 this domain reaches.
    If you cannot state the capability in one sentence, the domain is not yet a domain.
  >>
  EXPECT TEXT
  VALIDATE "a capability, not a field"
END STAGE

STAGE INTERFACE
  VERB CREATE
  SHAPE TEXT
  ASK <<
    Write the capability surface as function signatures only. D1: no bodies, no
    implementation named anywhere in this file.
    Every operation must be one a mock can satisfy with nothing attached.
    If an operation cannot be mocked, it is not a capability, it is a device.
  >>
  EXPECT TEXT
END STAGE

STAGE CONFORMANCE
  VERB MEASURE
  SHAPE JSON
  ASK <<
    List the conditions any implementation must satisfy. For each: id, condition,
    criterion, unit, and the source the number came from.
    Where the limit is not known, write exactly: not established.
    An invented limit is worse than an absent one, and a criterion with no unit is
    not a criterion.
  >>
  EXPECT JSON
  VALIDATE "every criterion has a unit or says not established"
END STAGE

STAGE PORTS
  VERB CREATE
  SHAPE LIST
  ASK <<
    List the substrates this interface will be realised on. Two are mandatory: mock,
    and template. Name what each remaining port exists to reach, and what it cannot do.
  >>
  EXPECT LIST
END STAGE

STAGE CORRELATE
  VERB INTEGRATE
  SHAPE JSON
  ASK <<
    Declare the correlations. For each: with, kind (shares_primitive, consumes,
    supplies, co_located, same_lattice_point, mounts_in), and exactly what is shared.
    A shared primitive must be declared from BOTH ends. If the other end has not
    declared it, the relation is a proposal, not a correlation — mark it so.
    Do not claim a relation because two things sound related.
  >>
  EXPECT JSON
END STAGE

STAGE ROADMAP
  VERB CREATE
  SHAPE JSON
  ASK <<
    Break the domain into packages. Each: id, track, deps, owns (paths), brief,
    acceptance (commands that must exit 0).
    At least one package must have no dependencies, or nobody can start.
    A package whose acceptance is "review it" is not a package.
  >>
  EXPECT JSON
END STAGE

STAGE FALSIFY
  VERB FALSIFY
  SHAPE TEXT
  ASK <<
    Try to break your own descriptor. Name the vocabulary you borrowed from another
    domain. Name the conformance number you cannot source. Name the package you could
    not actually start tomorrow.
    Report what you found, not that you looked.
  >>
  EXPECT TEXT
END STAGE

STAGE SEAL
  VERB VERIFY
  SHAPE TEXT
  ASK <<
    Run: python3 tools/spine_validate.py <descriptor> --repo <tree>
    Then: python3 tools/spine_leak.py <all descriptors>
    Paste both outputs verbatim. Not a summary of them.
  >>
  EXPECT TEXT
  GATE "SEAL domain"
END STAGE
